From 2168817aa1d55e66e7d7047a3e845855508d5b85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sento Daimon <339524263+sentodaimon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:18:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Coin Series stage 2: RandomX proof of work with five-chain
 merged mining

- vendored RandomX (src/randomx, BSD 3-Clause), linked into bitcoin_common
- Coin Series header: 76-byte body + 3 merge-tree siblings + 64-bit nonce (180 bytes);
  Bitcoin 80-byte format unchanged when no -coin is selected
- PoW: commitment = SHA256d(tag || body), 8-leaf merge tree (slot per chain),
  key = SHA256(tag || nTime/1209600), RandomX(key, root || nonce64) <= target
- RandomX version 1 or 2 selectable (-randomxversion, development only)
- block index / disk index / headers sync carry the new fields
- RPC: getmergework, submitmergework; getblockheader shows nonce64 and mergebranch
- contrib/coinseries/merge_miner.py reference merged miner (RandomX via shared library)
- tests: header format, merge tree, key epochs, PoW accept/reject (v1, v2),
  merged-mining smoke test (restart reload, P2P sync)
